    broadcast_to
    broadcast_shapes

    Examples
    --------

    Manually adding two vectors, using broadcasting:

    >>> import numpy as np
    >>> x = np.array([[1], [2], [3]])
    >>> y = np.array([4, 5, 6])
    >>> b = np.broadcast(x, y)

    >>> out = np.empty(b.shape)
    >>> out.flat = [u+v for (u,v) in b]
    >>> out
    array([[5.,  6.,  7.],
           [6.,  7.,  8.],
           [7.,  8.,  9.]])

