    Get the projected size along a given normal for an array of vectors.

    >>> v = np.array([[0., 5., 0.], [0., 0., 10.], [0., 6., 8.]])
    >>> n = np.array([0., 0.6, 0.8])
    >>> np.vecdot(v, n)
    array([ 3.,  8., 10.])

